          "title": "First Look at LiveViewJS w/ Donnie Flood",
          "duration": "5:37:56",
          "channel": "Ryan Carniato",
          "description": "I spend a lot of time looking at declarative JavaScript frameworks. Looking at how they Server Render and are moving forward into a new hybrid future. But I've neglected looking at progress from backend technologies.\r\n\r\nDonnie Flood, creator of LiveViewJS, joins us to show how we can use LiveViews inspired by Phoenix Liveview in a full JavaScript stack.\n\n[0:00] Introduction\n[8:50] Welcome Donnie Flood\n[33:06] What is a LiveView?\n[35:28] Stateful Servers?\n[39:52] Do we always go to the Server on any Change?\n[43:16] LiveViewJS Origins\n[47:50] Routing\n[56:09] Application entry\n[1:02:57] The anatomy of a LiveView\n[1:13:21] Data Structure and Diffing\n[1:25:20] Leveraging Websockets\n[1:35:00] Forms\n[1:52:16] Does it Scale?\n[2:06:06} Hackernews\n[2:27:08] Exploring Client Performance\n[3:04:28] Wrapping up with Donny\n[3:09:35] Reflections on LiveViewJS\n[3:29:04] This Week in JavaScript\n\r\nThumbnail Image Credit: © Warner Bros. Pictures/IMDb",
